# Everything personal lives in data/ and none of it belongs in the repo:
#   config.json   the Anthropic and Wise Old Man API keys, the tracked account
#                 names, per-player colours, and the dashboard's port and
#                 network settings
#   wom.db        every snapshot of every account, and the written summaries
#   wom.log       run history, which names accounts as it updates them
#   *_prompt.txt  your tuned prompts, which tend to mention accounts by name
#
# The app recreates this directory on first run, writing the defaults from
# wom/config.py and wom/summaries.py.
data/

# assets/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The Dockerfile copies it, so leaving it
# out of the repo made `fly deploy` work only from a machine that happened to
# have run fetch_icons.py - a clean clone failed the build. 311KB is a fair
# price for a deploy that does not depend on the working directory.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Stray databases and logs outside data/, in case anything is ever pointed
# somewhere else - these must never be committed by accident.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log

# Editors and operating systems, and the local dev-server config that goes
# with them: which port to preview on is a property of a machine, not of the
# project.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Database copies pulled down by backup.py - the whole point is that they are
# not in the repo.
backups/

# Test artefacts
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
